  "Welcome to Duitful": "欢迎使用 Duitful",
  "A quick tour so you know where everything lives.": "快速导览，让你知道每样东西在哪里。",
  "<p>Duitful is a private money &amp; debt tracker. Everything stays on this device, encrypted with your passcode — there's no account and no server.</p> <p>This tour takes about a minute. You'll learn the difference between income, recurring bills, debts, and daily spending — then you're set.</p>": "<p>Duitful 是一个私密的记账和还债工具。所有资料都只留在这部设备上，用你的密码加密——不需要账户，也没有服务器。</p> <p>这个导览大约一分钟。你会搞清楚收入、固定账单、债务和日常支出的分别——然后就可以开始了。</p>",
  "How Duitful sees your money": "Duitful 怎么看你的钱",
  "Five buckets. Each one has its own tab.": "分成五类，每一类都有自己的页面。",
  "<p>Everything you track falls into one of these:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Income</strong> — money coming in. <em>Salary</em> (every month) or a <em>bonus</em> (one-off).</li> <li><strong>Recurring bills</strong> — fixed monthly costs that repeat. <em>Netflix, rent, internet.</em></li> <li><strong>Debts</strong> — money you owe that pays down and <em>ends</em>. <em>Car loan, PTPTN, credit card.</em></li> <li><strong>Daily spending</strong> — variable day-to-day. <em>Mamak, Grab, groceries.</em></li> <li><strong>Savings</strong> — goals you put money toward. <em>Emergency fund, Umrah.</em></li> </ul> <p>The key difference: a <strong>bill repeats forever</strong> (Netflix), a <strong>debt has an end</strong> (the car loan finishes once it's paid).</p>": "<p>你记的每一笔都属于以下其中一类：</p> <ul> <li><strong>收入</strong>——进账的钱。<em>工资</em> (每月) 或<em>花红</em> (一次性)。</li> <li><strong>固定账单</strong>——每月重复的固定开销。<em>Netflix、房租、网络。</em></li> <li><strong>债务</strong>——欠的钱，越还越少，<em>总会还完</em>。<em>车贷、PTPTN、信用卡。</em></li> <li><strong>日常支出</strong>——每天不固定的花费。<em>嘛嘛档、Grab、日常杂货。</em></li> <li><strong>储蓄</strong>——你存钱要达成的目标。<em>紧急备用金、朝觐。</em></li> </ul> <p>最大的分别：<strong>账单会一直重复</strong> (Netflix)，<strong>债务总有还完的一天</strong> (车贷还清就结束)。</p>",
  "Salary repeats; a bonus doesn't.": "工资每月都有，花红不会。",
  "<p>Enter what comes in each month. The <strong>Repeat next month</strong> tick decides the type:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Salary</strong> → leave <em>Repeat next month</em> ticked, so it carries forward automatically.</li> <li><strong>Bonus / gift</strong> → untick it — it only counts this month.</li> </ul>": "<p>填上每个月的进账。<strong>下个月重复</strong>的勾选决定类型：</p> <ul> <li><strong>工资</strong> → 保留<em>下个月重复</em>，会自动带到下个月。</li> <li><strong>花红 / 礼金</strong> → 取消勾选——只算这个月。</li> </ul>",
  "Add recurring bills": "添加固定账单",
  "The fixed costs that come every month.": "每个月都会来的固定开销。",
  "<p>Rent, internet, phone, Netflix, insurance — anything with a fixed monthly amount.</p> <p>Keep <strong>Repeat next month</strong> ticked so they reappear automatically. These never \"end\" — that's what makes them a bill and not a debt.</p>": "<p>房租、网络、电话、Netflix、保险——任何每月金额固定的开销。</p> <p>保留<strong>下个月重复</strong>的勾选，就会自动再出现。账单永远不会“还完”——这就是账单和债务的分别。</p>",
  "Add your debts": "添加你的债务",
  "A debt has a balance — and an end.": "债务有余额——也有还完的一天。",
  "<p>Unlike a bill, a debt has a <strong>balance that shrinks</strong> as you pay it down. Car loan, PTPTN, credit card, BNPL.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Standard</strong> — credit cards, personal/car loans (balance + APR + minimum).</li> <li><strong>Installment</strong> — Atome, SPayLater (fixed monthly, set number of months).</li> </ul> <p>Duitful pays the <strong>highest-APR debt first</strong> (the avalanche method) and shows your debt-free date.</p>": "<p>和账单不同，债务有<strong>越还越少的余额</strong>。车贷、PTPTN、信用卡、先买后付。</p> <ul> <li><strong>一般</strong>——信用卡、个人/汽车贷款 (余额 + 年利率 + 最低还款)。</li> <li><strong>分期付款</strong>——Atome、SPayLater (每月固定金额，固定期数)。</li> </ul> <p>Duitful 会<strong>先还年利率最高的债务</strong> (雪崩法)，并告诉你哪天能还清。</p>",
  "Log daily spending": "记录日常支出",
  "Spend, pay a debt, or save — in one tap.": "支出、还债或存钱——一点就记。",
  "<p>This is your day-to-day: mamak, Grab, groceries. Pick the type, type the amount, hit Save.</p> <ul> <li><strong>Spend</strong> — a normal expense (food, transport, shopping).</li> <li><strong>Pay debt</strong> — a payment toward a debt you added.</li> <li><strong>Save</strong> — a deposit into a savings goal.</li> </ul>": "<p>这是你的日常：嘛嘛档、Grab、日常杂货。选类型、输入金额、按保存。</p> <ul> <li><strong>支出</strong>——一般开销 (餐饮、交通、购物)。</li> <li><strong>还债</strong>——还你添加过的债务。</li> <li><strong>存钱</strong>——存入储蓄目标。</li> </ul>",
  "Scan a receipt": "扫描收据",
  "Snap it, we read the amount.": "拍下来，我们帮你读出金额。",
  "<p>Tap <strong>Scan receipt</strong> to take a photo (or pick one from your gallery). Duitful reads the total on-device — the image never leaves your phone.</p> <p>Free includes 5 scans a month; Pro scans without a limit, and so does the optional 14-day trial.</p>": "<p>点<strong>扫描收据</strong>拍照 (或从相册选)。Duitful 在手机上读取总额——图片绝不离开你的手机。</p> <p>免费版每月 5 次；Pro 不限次数，可选的 14 天试用也一样。</p>",
  "Set a savings goal": "设定储蓄目标",
  "Emergency fund, Umrah, a new phone.": "紧急备用金、朝觐、新手机。",
  "<p>Set a target, then log deposits from Home with <strong>Save</strong>.</p>": "<p>设定目标，然后在首页用<strong>存钱</strong>记录存款。</p>",
  "Your balance at a glance": "一眼看余额",
  "Back on Home — the number that matters.": "回到首页——最重要的那个数字。",
  "<p>The hero card shows <strong>balance left this month</strong>: income minus recurring bills, minimum debt payments, and daily spending.</p> <p>Below it, the per-day line tells you roughly how much you can spend to stay on track.</p>": "<p>主卡片显示<strong>本月剩余</strong>：收入减去固定账单、最低还款和日常支出。</p> <p>下面那一行告诉你每天大概能花多少，才能撑到月底。</p>",
  "Settings — you own the data": "设置——资料归你所有",
  "Theme, backup, reminders, passcode.": "主题、备份、提醒、密码。",
  "<p>Here you can switch <strong>Light / Dark</strong> theme, export a CSV backup, set reminders, change your passcode, and manage Pro.</p> <p>Everything is encrypted on this device only. <strong>Losing your passcode means losing the data</strong>, so export a CSV somewhere safe.</p>": "<p>在这里可以切换<strong>浅色 / 深色</strong>主题、导出 CSV 备份、设置提醒、更改密码和管理 Pro。</p> <p>所有资料只在这部设备上加密保存。<strong>忘了密码就等于丢了资料</strong>，所以请把 CSV 导出存到安全的地方。</p>",
